---
import LearnLayout from "../../components/LearnLayout.astro";
---

<LearnLayout
  title="Resources: Links & Notes Without a Tab — Learn — cntxt"
  description="How to attach manually-saved links and notes to a Project or Quest, separate from its live tabs."
  path="/learn/resources"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Resources: links & notes without a tab</h1>
  <p>
    Not everything worth keeping needs an open tab. A Resource is a
    manually-saved link or note attached directly to a Project or a Quest —
    reference material you want next to your work without it counting as
    one of your live tabs.
  </p>
  <p>
    A Resource belongs to exactly one Quest or one Project. Saving a
    Quest-scoped Resource onto its parent Project is how it survives that
    Quest being deleted later.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <table class="status-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Manually-added links/notes attached to a Project or Quest</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</LearnLayout>
